      "content": "Exactly. That's what I'm getting at. It seems like the whole ideology is built on a house of cards because it can't account for basic human nature or property rights. If you really look at it, isn't it just fundamentally incompatible with a free society? Why do they even try to argue that it can work in a modern economy when those contradictions are so glaring? It feels like they're just ignoring reality to push a specific agenda.",
